{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MnnRSptP6t2tugE8nw4iXH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the situation is:\n- L3 has C01-C07 (7 CUs), KA files exist for C01-C04 only\n- L4 has C01-C06 (6 CUs), no KA files\n- L5 has C01-C07 (7 CUs), no KA files\n- Most CU folders beyond L3-C04 are empty\n\nThe previous attempt produced 3414 lines - way over the 500 limit. I need to keep the entire implementation (script + test) under 500 total lines of diff.\n\nKey strategy: Make the script EXTREMELY compact. \n\nI'm going to strip this down to a bare-bones scanner that walks the IT directories, checks for KA.md files, validates they have at least 12 questions plus an answer scheme and rubric, then outputs a simple completeness matrix showing which levels/CUs are covered and what needs remediation.\n\nFor the 500-line diff budget, I'm targeting around 80-90 lines for the script itself, 60-70 for tests, and just a couple lines to update prd.json—that should keep me well under the limit while still hitting all the acceptance criteria.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2541,"cache_read_input_tokens":34519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2541},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41856400-6278-4fe8-b4e8-d6ce57744942","uuid":"29547c85-a62c-473d-b614-8f197efaab33"}
