{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YN9QSxCUxmEfG3oma2nVZJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Tests for NOSS-to-WIM Competency-to-Assessment Coverage Validator (US-022).\"\"\"\n2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n3\t\n4\timport subprocess\n5\timport sys\n6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n7\t\n8\tPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).parent.parent\n9\tVALIDATOR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"_tools\" / \"coverage_validator.py\"\n10\t\n11\t\n12\tdef _run(subject: str, out: Path | None = None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n13\t    cmd = [sys.executable, str(VALIDATOR), \"--subject\", subject, \"--root\", str(PROJECT_ROOT)]\n14\t    if out:\n15\t        cmd += [\"--output\", str(out)]\n16\t    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n17\t\n18\t\n19\tdef test_no_unmapped_activities(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n20\t    \"\"\"All BEV work activities and knowledge items map to existing WIM documents.\"\"\"\n21\t    out = tmp_path / \"gap-report.txt\"\n22\t    result = _run(\"BEV\", out)\n23\t    assert result.returncode == 0, (\n24\t        f\"BEV coverage gaps found:\\n{out.read_text(encoding='utf-8') if out.exists() else result.stdout}\"\n25\t    )\n26\t    report = out.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n27\t    assert \"Not Covered\" not in report or \"0 items\" in report or \"All documents covered\" in report\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tdef test_all_subjects_run_without_error(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n31\t    \"\"\"Validator runs for --subject all and creates report file.\"\"\"\n32\t    out = tmp_path / \"all-subjects.txt\"\n33\t    result = _run(\"all\", out)\n34\t    assert out.exists(), \"Output file not created\"\n35\t    report = out.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n36\t    assert \"BEV\" in report\n37\t    assert \"Aesthetic\" in report\n38\t    assert \"IT\" in report\n39\t    # Exit code 0 means zero gaps; 1 means gaps exist — both are valid runs (not crashes)\n40\t    assert result.returncode in (0, 1), f\"Unexpected exit code: {result.returncode}\\n{result.stderr}\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41856400-6278-4fe8-b4e8-d6ce57744942","uuid":"bdcd08f3-01e1-4ab6-a386-30967f2640f7","timestamp":"2026-04-17T03:57:30.210Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\tests\\test_coverage_validator.py","content":"\"\"\"Tests for NOSS-to-WIM Competency-to-Assessment Coverage Validator (US-022).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).parent.parent\nVALIDATOR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"_tools\" / \"coverage_validator.py\"\n\n\ndef _run(subject: str, out: Path | None = None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:\n    cmd = [sys.executable, str(VALIDATOR), \"--subject\", subject, \"--root\", str(PROJECT_ROOT)]\n    if out:\n        cmd += [\"--output\", str(out)]\n    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n\ndef test_no_unmapped_activities(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"All BEV work activities and knowledge items map to existing WIM documents.\"\"\"\n    out = tmp_path / \"gap-report.txt\"\n    result = _run(\"BEV\", out)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, (\n        f\"BEV coverage gaps found:\\n{out.read_text(encoding='utf-8') if out.exists() else result.stdout}\"\n    )\n    report = out.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    assert \"Not Covered\" not in report or \"0 items\" in report or \"All documents covered\" in report\n\n\ndef test_all_subjects_run_without_error(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validator runs for --subject all and creates report file.\"\"\"\n    out = tmp_path / \"all-subjects.txt\"\n    result = _run(\"all\", out)\n    assert out.exists(), \"Output file not created\"\n    report = out.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    assert \"BEV\" in report\n    assert \"Aesthetic\" in report\n    assert \"IT\" in report\n    # Exit code 0 means zero gaps; 1 means gaps exist — both are valid runs (not crashes)\n    assert result.returncode in (0, 1), f\"Unexpected exit code: {result.returncode}\\n{result.stderr}\"","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BE1iMB66EpJcYgtk3mrHTF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KA — IT-020-3:2013-C03 Computer System Repair\n2\t\n3\t**Kod:** IT-020-3:2013-C03/KA | **Tahap:** 3 | **Kertas Warna:** Pink\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t### Q1 — Repair Job Order\n8\t**Type:** MCQ | **Difficulty:** L1 | **Marks:** 2 | **LO Ref:** WA1.K1\n9\t\n10\tWhich field is MOST critical when assessing a computer repair job order?\n11\t\n12\t(a) User's department name  (b) Asset ID and fault description  (c) Monitor brand  (d) Printer serial number\n13\t\n14\t**Answer:** (b)  **Rubric:** 3=Correct+justification | 2=Correct | 1=Partially correct | 0=Wrong\n15\t\n16\t---\n17\t\n18\t### Q2 — Online Troubleshooting\n19\t**Type:** MCQ | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 2 | **LO Ref:** WA2.K2\n20\t\n21\tA technician uses remote desktop software to resolve a fault. Which condition is REQUIRED?\n22\t\n23\t(a) The user's PC must be powered off  (b) The technician must be on-site\n24\t(c) The user's PC must be booted and on the network  (d) The PC must have a GPU installed\n25\t\n26\t**Answer:** (c)  **Rubric:** 3=Correct+explanation | 2=Correct | 1=Partially correct | 0=Wrong\n27\t\n28\t---\n29\t\n30\t### Q3 — PSU Fault Diagnosis\n31\t**Type:** Short Answer | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 4 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K4\n32\t\n33\tState THREE checks a technician performs to diagnose a suspected faulty PSU using a multimeter.\n34\t\n35\t**Model Answer:** (1) Measure +12 V rail at the ATX connector — should read 11.4–12.6 V.\n36\t(2) Measure +5 V rail — should read 4.75–5.25 V. (3) Measure +3.3 V rail — should read 3.135–3.465 V.\n37\tAny reading outside spec confirms PSU fault.\n38\t\n39\t**Rubric:** 3=3 voltage checks with acceptable ranges | 2=2 correct checks | 1=1 correct check | 0=Wrong/blank\n40\t\n41\t---\n42\t\n43\t### Q4 — RAM Fault Diagnosis\n44\t**Type:** Short Answer | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 4 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K4\n45\t\n46\tDescribe the steps to diagnose faulty RAM in a system that fails to POST.\n47\t\n48\t**Model Answer:** (1) Reseat all RAM modules firmly. (2) Test with one stick in slot 1; try each stick\n49\tindividually. (3) Run Memtest86 from bootable USB to confirm errors. (4) Replace any stick that\n50\tshows errors; record module serial number in status report.\n51\t\n52\t**Rubric:** 3=All 4 steps correct | 2=Steps 1–3 correct | 1=Reseat only | 0=Incorrect/blank\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t### Q5 — On-Site Repair Scenario\n57\t**Type:** Scenario | **Difficulty:** L3 | **Marks:** 8 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K1-K5\n58\t\n59\t**Scenario:** A user reports \"no display\" after the PC was moved to a new desk. The PC powers on\n60\t(fans spin, power LED lit) but the monitor shows no signal. Online troubleshooting was not able to\n61\tresolve it. You are dispatched for on-site repair.\n62\t\n63\t(a) List FOUR diagnostic steps you would perform on-site, in sequence. (4 marks)\n64\t(b) Describe FOUR items you would record in the computer status report. (4 marks)\n65\t\n66\t**Rubric:** 3=4 steps+4 report items | 2=3 steps+3 items | 1=1–2 steps | 0=Incorrect/blank\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41856400-6278-4fe8-b4e8-d6ce57744942","uuid":"4905c87d-0923-4d72-9a47-2b4ebf9f0bb6","timestamp":"2026-04-17T03:57:30.219Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\it-computer-system\\L3-C03\\KA.md","content":"# KA — IT-020-3:2013-C03 Computer System Repair\n\n**Kod:** IT-020-3:2013-C03/KA | **Tahap:** 3 | **Kertas Warna:** Pink\n\n---\n\n### Q1 — Repair Job Order\n**Type:** MCQ | **Difficulty:** L1 | **Marks:** 2 | **LO Ref:** WA1.K1\n\nWhich field is MOST critical when assessing a computer repair job order?\n\n(a) User's department name  (b) Asset ID and fault description  (c) Monitor brand  (d) Printer serial number\n\n**Answer:** (b)  **Rubric:** 3=Correct+justification | 2=Correct | 1=Partially correct | 0=Wrong\n\n---\n\n### Q2 — Online Troubleshooting\n**Type:** MCQ | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 2 | **LO Ref:** WA2.K2\n\nA technician uses remote desktop software to resolve a fault. Which condition is REQUIRED?\n\n(a) The user's PC must be powered off  (b) The technician must be on-site\n(c) The user's PC must be booted and on the network  (d) The PC must have a GPU installed\n\n**Answer:** (c)  **Rubric:** 3=Correct+explanation | 2=Correct | 1=Partially correct | 0=Wrong\n\n---\n\n### Q3 — PSU Fault Diagnosis\n**Type:** Short Answer | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 4 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K4\n\nState THREE checks a technician performs to diagnose a suspected faulty PSU using a multimeter.\n\n**Model Answer:** (1) Measure +12 V rail at the ATX connector — should read 11.4–12.6 V.\n(2) Measure +5 V rail — should read 4.75–5.25 V. (3) Measure +3.3 V rail — should read 3.135–3.465 V.\nAny reading outside spec confirms PSU fault.\n\n**Rubric:** 3=3 voltage checks with acceptable ranges | 2=2 correct checks | 1=1 correct check | 0=Wrong/blank\n\n---\n\n### Q4 — RAM Fault Diagnosis\n**Type:** Short Answer | **Difficulty:** L2 | **Marks:** 4 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K4\n\nDescribe the steps to diagnose faulty RAM in a system that fails to POST.\n\n**Model Answer:** (1) Reseat all RAM modules firmly. (2) Test with one stick in slot 1; try each stick\nindividually. (3) Run Memtest86 from bootable USB to confirm errors. (4) Replace any stick that\nshows errors; record module serial number in status report.\n\n**Rubric:** 3=All 4 steps correct | 2=Steps 1–3 correct | 1=Reseat only | 0=Incorrect/blank\n\n---\n\n### Q5 — On-Site Repair Scenario\n**Type:** Scenario | **Difficulty:** L3 | **Marks:** 8 | **LO Ref:** WA3.K1-K5\n\n**Scenario:** A user reports \"no display\" after the PC was moved to a new desk. The PC powers on\n(fans spin, power LED lit) but the monitor shows no signal. Online troubleshooting was not able to\nresolve it. You are dispatched for on-site repair.\n\n(a) List FOUR diagnostic steps you would perform on-site, in sequence. (4 marks)\n(b) Describe FOUR items you would record in the computer status report. (4 marks)\n\n**Rubric:** 3=4 steps+4 report items | 2=3 steps+3 items | 1=1–2 steps | 0=Incorrect/blank\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
