{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GzKMeyWViG7XfiU5vJifVC","type":"tool_result","content":"38\t\n39\t## BAHAGIAN A: SOALAN PELBAGAI PILIHAN / SECTION A: MULTIPLE CHOICE (30 marks)\n40\t\n41\tAnswer all 15 questions. Each question carries 2 marks. Circle the correct answer.\n42\t\n43\t**1.** The document that formally initiates a computer system set-up task is called a:\n44\t\n45\t- (a) Purchase order\n46\t- (b) Job request / work order\n47\t- (c) Delivery note\n48\t- (d) Invoice\n49\t\n50\t**2.** Which of the following is a correct ESD prevention measure?\n51\t\n52\t- (a) Working in a dry room without any grounding\n53\t- (b) Wearing an anti-static wrist strap connected to a grounded point\n54\t- (c) Handling the motherboard by its circuit traces\n55\t- (d) Using a standard vacuum cleaner on the motherboard\n56\t\n57\t**3.** The CPU socket type must match between the:\n58\t\n59\t- (a) CPU and RAM\n60\t- (b) CPU and motherboard\n61\t- (c) PSU and monitor\n62\t- (d) Storage drive and keyboard\n63\t\n64\t**4.** Thermal paste is applied between the CPU and heatsink to:\n65\t\n66\t- (a) Permanently glue them together\n67\t- (b) Fill microscopic gaps for efficient heat transfer\n68\t- (c) Make the CPU run at a higher speed\n69\t- (d) Prevent the CPU from being removed\n70\t\n71\t**5.** For dual-channel RAM operation, modules should be installed in:\n72\t\n73\t- (a) Any random slots\n74\t- (b) Matched paired slots as per the motherboard manual\n75\t- (c) A single slot only\n76\t- (d) The slot closest to the CPU\n77\t\n78\t**6.** NVMe Gen5 storage drives connect via:\n79\t\n80\t- (a) SATA data cable\n81\t- (b) M.2 PCIe Gen5 slot on the motherboard\n82\t- (c) USB 3.0 port\n83\t- (d) IDE ribbon cable\n84\t\n85\t**7.** The recommended order for driver installation after OS setup is:\n86\t\n87\t- (a) Audio > GPU > Chipset"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41856400-6278-4fe8-b4e8-d6ce57744942","uuid":"9e210922-c455-413b-a4f0-3df999505512","timestamp":"2026-04-17T03:58:52.005Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\it-computer-system\\L3-C01\\KA.md","content":"\n## BAHAGIAN A: SOALAN PELBAGAI PILIHAN / SECTION A: MULTIPLE CHOICE (30 marks)\n\nAnswer all 15 questions. Each question carries 2 marks. Circle the correct answer.\n\n**1.** The document that formally initiates a computer system set-up task is called a:\n\n- (a) Purchase order\n- (b) Job request / work order\n- (c) Delivery note\n- (d) Invoice\n\n**2.** Which of the following is a correct ESD prevention measure?\n\n- (a) Working in a dry room without any grounding\n- (b) Wearing an anti-static wrist strap connected to a grounded point\n- (c) Handling the motherboard by its circuit traces\n- (d) Using a standard vacuum cleaner on the motherboard\n\n**3.** The CPU socket type must match between the:\n\n- (a) CPU and RAM\n- (b) CPU and motherboard\n- (c) PSU and monitor\n- (d) Storage drive and keyboard\n\n**4.** Thermal paste is applied between the CPU and heatsink to:\n\n- (a) Permanently glue them together\n- (b) Fill microscopic gaps for efficient heat transfer\n- (c) Make the CPU run at a higher speed\n- (d) Prevent the CPU from being removed\n\n**5.** For dual-channel RAM operation, modules should be installed in:\n\n- (a) Any random slots\n- (b) Matched paired slots as per the motherboard manual\n- (c) A single slot only\n- (d) The slot closest to the CPU\n\n**6.** NVMe Gen5 storage drives connect via:\n\n- (a) SATA data cable\n- (b) M.2 PCIe Gen5 slot on the motherboard\n- (c) USB 3.0 port\n- (d) IDE ribbon cable\n\n**7.** The recommended order for driver installation after OS setup is:\n\n- (a) Audio > GPU > Chipset","numLines":50,"startLine":38,"totalLines":205}}}
